@attribute [CustomPage("Components/Layout/Overview")]

<h1>Layout</h1>

<h2><code>Card</code></h2>
<p>A bordered, rounded surface that holds whatever it is given in <code>ChildContent</code>.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>Title</code>: a bold heading at the top. Null shows a plain card with no heading and no aside.</li>
    <li><code>Aside</code>: muted text at the right of the title, e.g. "1 this week". It stays on one line. Only shown with a title.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>TestId</code>, and <code>{TestId}-aside</code> on the aside.</li>
</ul>

<p>Stories: <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-card--docs">Card</a></p>

<h2><code>BottomNav</code></h2>
<p>The bar at the foot of a screen: the tabs in <code>Items</code> with a raised button between them. The tab equal to <code>Current</code> has a pill behind its icon, bold text and <code>aria-current="page"</code>; tapping it raises nothing. With an odd number of tabs the extra one goes left of the raised button.</p>
<ul>
    <li><code>AddLabel</code> and <code>AddIcon</code>: the raised button, a primary rounded square (<code>--radius-md</code>) of <code>--add-button-size</code>, lifted by <code>--add-button-lift</code> so its label is level with the tab labels. It is an action and is never current.</li>
    <li><code>AddHasPopup</code>: optional <code>aria-haspopup</code> value, e.g. <code>dialog</code>.</li>
    <li><code>OnNavigate</code> is raised with the tapped tab; <code>OnAdd</code> by the raised button.</li>
    <li><code>data-testid</code>: <code>bottom-nav</code>, <code>add-button</code> and each item's <code>TestId</code>.</li>
</ul>

<p>Stories: <a href="./?path=/docs/components-layout-bottomnav--docs">BottomNav</a></p>
